  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> be positive real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be a point in the first quadrant that lies on the hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Suppose the tangent to the hyperbola at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> and suppose the normal to the hyperbola at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> cuts off equal intercepts on the coordinate axes. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi></math> denote the area of the triangle formed by the tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, the normal at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> -axis. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math> denotes the eccentricity of the hyperbola, then which of the following statements is/are TRUE?",
    "image": null
  },
